>> Belatedly, a thought occurred to me-- don't Vampire Lords levitate?  Has
>> anybody ever tried walking the moat as a Vampire Lord?
>
>Number-one choice.  They levitate, wear armor and use weapons (the other
>characteristics aren't that useful).

Since the duration of your polymorph depends on the ratio of your level /
the level of the critter you 'morph into, you may not be a vampire lord
long enough to levitate everywhere you want.

To make your 'morph last, 'morph into a low level critter.  A floating
eye excels in that catagory.

Everyone here loves 'morphing into Vampire Lords.  If you ask me nothing can
beat a marilith for the damage factor.  (Who needs armor when you get
5 attacks with an artifact?)  (Which, by the way, should be modified so
that a marilith can wield 5 different weapons, and attacks with each.)

